OrionLayer open fix 79 — the battle's sounds as events, the engine silent while a client draws
==============================================================================================

Work order 212 (Part C, Data's decision 1: option B of work order 210, then
fix 71). orion2re on `orionlayer-local`, on top of e75477c5 (open fix 74).
Every line under ORION2RE_EXT.

The hidden engine played every battle sound itself, at its own time, before
the client's picture of it (work order 210: 0.25 s ahead for a beam, the
whole 2.5 s of the Stellar Converter). While a battle is live, the window
hidden and a client connected, `ERICNET::Mox_Play_Sound_` now records the
sound as CEV_SOUND (its SOUND.LBX entry, a handle of its own 16-127 that is
never a channel, the 55 ms ticks waited since the event before) instead of
playing it, and `Fadeout_Sound_`, `Loop_Sound_` and `Pitch_Bend_Sound_` of
such a handle record CEV_SOUND_CHANGE (handle, 1 fade / 2 loop / 3 pitch,
value, ticks) and touch no channel; a fade of -1 is recorded and still done.
`timer::Release_Time_` counts its ticks for this whether it waits or not.
Only what the original would play is recorded (sound effects on, not super
fast); music streams are untouched; outside a battle nothing changes.

